{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock\/at(_:named:perform:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"at","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"time","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV","text":"TimeOfDay","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"named","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"name","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"perform","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"body","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@escaping ","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV","text":"TimedEvent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When it goes off."}]}],"name":"time"},{"name":"name","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The daemon’s name, unique across the whole game.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"body","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What happens."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The timed event, for the game’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The alarm fires ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"once","type":"text"}]},{"text":", at the end of the first turn on or after its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time — so a clock running several minutes per turn that steps over the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"target still fires, and so does one the host jumps forward by hand. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time earlier in the day than the clock’s start means ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"tomorrow"}]},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is what an overnight game wants.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Firing once is enforced by the alarm stopping its own daemon, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arming state is ordinary daemon state: it saves and restores for free,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"stopDaemon(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels an alarm that hasn’t fired, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"startDaemon(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-arms one that has."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timer names are global across a game, so prefix yours — the clock’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"convention is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"clock.<something>\""},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0